.TH CHM-TERMINAL-BRIDGE 1
.SH NAME
chm-terminal-bridge \- connect Aurora Web Terminal to a local workspace or shell
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 tools/runtime/chimera-terminal-backend.py
.RI [ --profile chimera|octavian ] [ --workspace DIRECTORY ] [ --port PORT ] [ --unsafe-shell ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts a loopback-only HTTP bridge for Aurora Terminal. Safe workspace mode is the default and does not invoke a shell. A one-time bearer token is printed at startup.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --profile PROFILE
Label this host as chimera or octavian. Default: chimera.
.TP
.B --workspace DIRECTORY
Workspace root for safe file operations. Default: ~/ChimeraTerminalWorkspace.
.TP
.B --port PORT
Loopback HTTP port. Default: 8767.
.TP
.B --unsafe-shell
Explicitly enable real local shell execution with current-user privileges. This is not a sandbox.
.SH SECURITY
Binds only to 127.0.0.1, requires a bearer token, restricts CORS and bounds command size, output and execution time.
